## ✅ Issue #18: Error Handling, Logging, and Route Exposure

### Centralized Error Handling

#### Created [exceptions.py](file:///c:/Users/Main/Downloads/ventics-ai-api-master/app/core/exceptions.py)

Custom exception hierarchy:
- [VenticsAPIException](file:///c:/Users/Main/Downloads/ventics-ai-api-master/app/core/exceptions.py#9-24) - Base exception
- [AuthenticationError](file:///c:/Users/Main/Downloads/ventics-ai-api-master/app/core/exceptions.py#26-36) - 401 errors
- [AuthorizationError](file:///c:/Users/Main/Downloads/ventics-ai-api-master/app/core/exceptions.py#45-55) - 403 errors
- [ValidationError](file:///c:/Users/Main/Downloads/ventics-ai-api-master/app/core/exceptions.py#57-70) - 422 errors
- [ResourceNotFoundError](file:///c:/Users/Main/Downloads/ventics-ai-api-master/app/core/exceptions.py#72-85) - 404 errors
- [ExternalServiceError](file:///c:/Users/Main/Downloads/ventics-ai-api-master/app/core/exceptions.py#87-99) - 502 errors
- [PaymentError](file:///c:/Users/Main/Downloads/ventics-ai-api-master/app/core/exceptions.py#101-114) - 402 errors
- [InsufficientCreditsError](file:///c:/Users/Main/Downloads/ventics-ai-api-master/app/core/exceptions.py#116-126) - 402 errors
- [RateLimitError](file:///c:/Users/Main/Downloads/ventics-ai-api-master/app/core/exceptions.py#128-138) - 429 errors
- [DatabaseError](file:///c:/Users/Main/Downloads/ventics-ai-api-master/app/core/exceptions.py#140-150) - 500 errors

Each exception includes:
- HTTP status code
- Error code (for client handling)
- User-friendly message
- Optional details dict (sanitized)

#### Created [error_handlers.py](file:///c:/Users/Main/Downloads/ventics-ai-api-master/app/core/error_handlers.py)

Standardized error responses:
```json
{
  "error": {
    "code": "AUTHENTICATION_FAILED",
    "message": "Invalid email or password",
    "request_id": "req_abc123",
    "timestamp": "2026-01-24T01:37:43Z"
  }
}
```

Features:
- Request ID tracking
- Automatic error logging with context
- Sanitized error messages (no stack traces to clients)
- Different handlers for different exception types

### Structured Logging

#### Created [logging_config.py](file:///c:/Users/Main/Downloads/ventics-ai-api-master/app/core/logging_config.py)

**JSON-formatted logs** (production):
```json
{
  "timestamp": "2026-01-24T01:37:43Z",
  "level": "INFO",
  "logger": "app.services.auth_service",
  "message": "User login successful",
  "request_id": "req_abc123",
  "user_id": "user_xyz",
  "endpoint": "/v1/auth/login",
  "duration_ms": 145
}
```

**Features:**
- Sensitive data filtering (passwords, tokens, API keys)
- Contextual logging (request_id, user_id, endpoint, duration)
- Configurable log levels per module
- Third-party library noise reduction

### Middleware

#### Created [middleware/__init__.py](file:///c:/Users/Main/Downloads/ventics-ai-api-master/app/middleware/__init__.py)

Three middleware components:

1. **RequestIDMiddleware**: Adds unique request ID to each request
2. **RequestLoggingMiddleware**: Logs all requests/responses with timing
3. **SecurityHeadersMiddleware**: Adds security headers
   - `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`
   - `X-Frame-Options: DENY`
   - `X-XSS-Protection: 1; mode=block`
   - `Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000`

#### Created [rate_limiter.py](file:///c:/Users/Main/Downloads/ventics-ai-api-master/app/middleware/rate_limiter.py)

**Rate Limiting Configuration:**
- Auth endpoints: 3-5 requests/minute
- Generation endpoints: 10 requests/minute
- Other endpoints: 100 requests/minute

Returns `429 Too Many Requests` with `Retry-After` header when exceeded.

