## ✅ Issue #19: Security - Authentication and API Configuration

### Security Configuration

#### Updated [config.py](file:///c:/Users/Main/Downloads/ventics-ai-api-master/app/core/config.py)

**New Security Settings:**
- `JWT_SECRET_KEY`: Now requires environment variable (validates on startup)
- `ALLOWED_ORIGINS`: Whitelist for CORS (comma-separated in .env)
- `REQUIRE_EMAIL_VERIFICATION`: Toggle for email verification
- `PASSWORD_MIN_LENGTH`: 8 characters
- `PASSWORD_REQUIRE_UPPERCASE/LOWERCASE/DIGIT/SPECIAL`: All true
- `RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED`: Toggle for rate limiting

**Security Validation:**
- Validates JWT secret is not default in production
- Validates JWT secret is at least 32 characters
- Validates CORS doesn't use wildcard in production
- Warns if Paystack webhook secret is missing

### CORS Configuration

#### Updated [main.py](file:///c:/Users/Main/Downloads/ventics-ai-api-master/app/main.py)

**Before (INSECURE):**
```python
allow_origins=["*"]  # ❌ Allows any origin
```

**After (SECURE):**
```python
allow_origins=settings.ALLOWED_ORIGINS  # ✅ Specific origins only
allow_methods=["GET", "POST", "PUT", "DELETE", "PATCH"]
allow_headers=["Authorization", "Content-Type", "X-Request-ID"]
max_age=600
```

### Authentication Improvements

#### Updated [auth_service.py](file:///c:/Users/Main/Downloads/ventics-ai-api-master/app/services/auth_service.py)

**Security Enhancements:**
- Uses custom exceptions instead of generic `ValueError`
- Generic error messages (don't reveal if email or password is wrong)
- Proper error handling for Google OAuth
- Database connection error handling

**Error Messages:**
- Before: "User with email not found" ❌ (reveals email exists)
- After: "Invalid email or password" ✅ (generic message)

### Environment Template

#### Created [.env.example](file:///c:/Users/Main/Downloads/ventics-ai-api-master/.env.example)

Comprehensive template with:
- All required environment variables
- Security warnings
- Example values (non-sensitive)
- Documentation for each section

